{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"account-default","id":"msg_011Cgyoxz2gJZBFrfM8hkpxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013AkWFzTK36iGg4KrKHUydD","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"verdict":"needs-human","reasons":["The plan updates aws_db_instance.orders, which is a database. The policy sends any database change to a human.","It's prod: the identifier is tallowmark-prod-orders. The instance class goes from db.r6g.large to db.r6g.xlarge. Resizing an RDS instance usually means a restart or a failover, so the orders database could be briefly down or degraded. That affects seat holds and checkout. Whether the change applies right away or in the next maintenance window depends on apply_immediately, which this plan doesn't show.","Nothing else is in the plan: no IAM wildcards, no buyer records changes and no lifecycle rules. It isn't an add-or-tag-only change, so it can't be auto-approved.","Before approving, a person should confirm the timing (maintenance window or apply_immediately), check whether the instance is Multi-AZ so a failover would be short, and check the cost and capacity reason for the resize."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":3401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66cde844-2c9e-4843-8bb7-af7033edd746","uuid":"88fb0571-98b8-45cb-8e7c-38b9c5a3b8d7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:19:07.220Z","request_id":"req_011CgyoxypncT1TNQM2iCSpR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013AkWFzTK36iGg4KrKHUydD":{"verdict":"needs-human","reasons":["The plan updates aws_db_instance.orders, which is a database. The policy sends any database change to a human.","It's prod: the identifier is tallowmark-prod-orders. The instance class goes from db.r6g.large to db.r6g.xlarge. Resizing an RDS instance usually means a restart or a failover, so the orders database could be briefly down or degraded. That affects seat holds and checkout. Whether the change applies right away or in the next maintenance window depends on apply_immediately, which this plan doesn't show.","Nothing else is in the plan: no IAM wildcards, no buyer records changes and no lifecycle rules. It isn't an add-or-tag-only change, so it can't be auto-approved.","Before approving, a person should confirm the timing (maintenance window or apply_immediately), check whether the instance is Multi-AZ so a failover would be short, and check the cost and capacity reason for the resize."]}}}
